      "message": "Can you change this API to:\n\n`VG_EXPORT int stream_renderer_snapshot_save(char *dir);`\n\nTwo reasons:\n\n1) That\u0027s the API rutabaga uses (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/crosvm/crosvm/+/4853266).  I think the test backend should use rutabaga.  The reason is then we can test additional context types (say a Rust only one) without having to boot a VM.  This will make the transition easier.\n\n2) I was doing another refactor/cleanup, and noticed GfxstreamEnd2EndTests have a dependency on AEMU base.  This leads to namespace collisions between `guest/android-emu/` and `hardware/google/aemu` with the cleanup.  I commented out the snapshot tests locally for it to build, but if the snapshot tests don\u0027t have such a reliance on AEMU base that would make it easier.  Having a reliance on AEMU base inside `libgfxstream_backend.so` is fine though.",
